</a></li><li>1972: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1972/11/20/recording-mixing-yang-yang-i-want-my-love-to-rest-tonight-approximately-infinite-universe-what-a-bastard-the-world-is-winter-song-yoko-ono/\">Recording, mixing: Yang Yang, I Want My Love To Rest Tonight, Approximately Infinite Universe, What A Bastard The World Is, Winter Song by Yoko Ono</a></li><li>1972: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1972/11/20/recording-little-lamb-dragonfly-wings-3/\">Recording: Little Lamb Dragonfly by Wings</a></li><li>1970: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1970/11/20/recording-little-lamb-dragonfly-wings-2/\">Recording: Little Lamb Dragonfly by Wings</a></li><li>1968: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1968/11/20/paul-mccartney-interview-radio-luxembourg/\">Paul McCartney is interviewed for Radio Luxembourg</a></li><li>1966: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1966/11/20/brian-epstein-party-four-tops-london/\">Brian Epstein holds a party for The Four Tops in London</a></li><li>1963: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1963/11/20/live-abc-cinema-manchester/\">The Beatles live: ABC Cinema, Manchester</a></li><li>1962: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1962/11/20/live-floral-hall-southport-2/\">The Beatles live: Floral Hall, Southport</a></li><li>1960: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1960/11/20/live-kaiserkeller-hamburg-48/\">The Beatles live: Kaiserkeller, Hamburg</a></li></ul><p>Want more? Visit the <a title=\"Day after day: the Beatles' history\" href=\"/history/\">Beatles history section</a>.</p></div><div class=\"gm-map\" style=\"position: relative;height: 390px; width: 100%;\"><iframe data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"about:blank\" name=\"gm-map-1\" allowfullscreen=\"\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/?geo_mashup_content=render-map&amp;map_data_key=703429cf9e62a89f7503f9e353b1c605&amp;height=390&amp;width=100%&amp;add_overview_control=false&amp;zoom=16&amp;enable_street_view=false&amp;map_type=G_HYBRID_MAP&amp;name=gm-map-1&amp;object_id=2495&amp;map_content=single\" style=\"position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; border: none; overflow: hidden;\" title=\"Geo Mashup Map\"></iframe></div>",
  "textContent": "Early in the morning John Lennon filmed part of a sequence for Dudley Moore’s forthcoming TV show Not Only… But Also. Filming took place on Wimbledon Common, and was complete by mid-morning. Lennon appeared with Moore and co-star Norman Rossington, to accompany a reading of Deaf Ted, Danoota, (and me) from In His Own Write.A second appearance was made at BBC Television Centre on 29 November 1964.The show was broadcast on Saturday 9 January 1965 at 9.20pm on BBC Two.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nPage last updated: 12 April 2018Also on this day...2011: Ringo Starr and his All-Starr Band live: Chevrolet Hall, Olinda2009: BBC screens Paul McCartney’s Children in Need appearance2009: Ringo Starr and Paul McCartney to reunite? Y Not!2005: Paul McCartney live: American Airlines Center, Dallas1981: UK album release: Stop And Smell The Roses by Ringo Starr1976: Mixing: Wings Over America by Wings1974: George Harrison live: St Louis Arena, St Louis1974: John Lennon watches Elton John perform in Boston1974: Television: Wings on Top Of The Pops1972: Recording, mixing: Yang Yang, I Want My Love To Rest Tonight, Approximately Infinite Universe, What A Bastard The World Is, Winter Song by Yoko Ono1972: Recording: Little Lamb Dragonfly by Wings1970: Recording: Little Lamb Dragonfly by Wings1968: Paul McCartney is interviewed for Radio Luxembourg1966: Brian Epstein holds a party for The Four Tops in London1963: The Beatles live: ABC Cinema, Manchester1962: The Beatles live: Floral Hall, Southport1960: The Beatles live: Kaiserkeller, HamburgWant more? Visit the Beatles history section.",
